      "locus": "Gebhardt VII.XIV (redactor: Secundulus; the handover)",
      "source_path": "/Users/stephansmac/SaneApps/clients/translations/books/perpetua-felicitas/translations/perpetua_source.json",
      "source_text": [
        "Hae uisiones insigniores ipsorum martyrum beatissimorum Saturi et Perpetuae, quas ipsi conscripserunt. Secundulum uero deus maturiore exitu de saeculo adhuc in carcere euocauit, non sine gratia, ut bestias lucraretur. Gladium tamen etsi non anima, certe caro eius agnouit."
      ],
      "english": [
        "These are the signal visions of the most blessed martyrs Saturus and Perpetua, which they themselves set down in writing. As for Secundulus, God summoned him from this world while he was still in prison by an earlier death, not without grace, sparing him the beasts. Yet though his soul did not meet it, his flesh certainly came to know the sword."
      ],
      "source_sha256": "4c88ed6593903110089c9bc61bcc14602973e24bd4e00212eace7c67561a8682",
